{"format": "SIDPULSE", "format_version": 8, "song": {"title": "Autumn at Five (Synthwave Mix / PCM Drums)", "author": "SIDpulse Tracker [CW/FF]", "comments": "Autumn at Five (Synthwave Mix)\nSource: examples/autumn-at-five.sidpulse from SIDpulse Tracker 0.2.23.\nOriginal composition: SIDpulse Tracker. Synthwave arrangement: ChaosWhisperer for Harry.\n91 BPM, D minor, 72 bars, approximately 3:10 before looping.\nThe source's full 32-bar melody is preserved in orders 04-13 (hex),\nincluding note pitches, starts and note-offs; its harmony and inversions remain.\nArrangement: 8-bar intro, 16-bar theme, 4-bar mist breakdown, 12-bar lift,\n24-bar brighter reprise, 8-bar outro. Reference influence: night_etc.mp3's\napproximately 91 BPM pulse, low-end emphasis, offbeats and nighttime pacing.\nNo melody or audio from the reference is embedded.\nCH1: PWM melody, quiet single-voice echoes and arps in the original rests.\nCH2: root/octave pulse motor; a triangle kick morphs into bass under each snare.\nSustained bass in the breakdown/outro. CH2/CH3 together supply four-on-the-floor.\nCH3: triangle kick, noise/pulse snare, hats and toms; chord arp in quiet sections.\nCTRL: one real shared low-pass filter for CH1/CH2, with beat-shaped opening.\nThree physical SID voices only. No samples, extra SID, external reverb or FX.\nPreferred chip: 8580. PAL file; separate NTSC timing variant accompanies it.\nAll instrument programs and automation are editable in the supplied tracker.\nF5 plays. F8 stops. F4 instruments. F11 arrangement. F12 timing/loop.\n\nPCM drum variant: instruments 03 and 04 override SID synthesis with embedded algorithmic kick/snare samples. Root notes match the existing drum notes. SID patch parameters remain stored; drum pitch/gate programs are bypassed. Instrument 16 remains the original kick-to-bass hybrid, preserving its bass line. Host preview and WAV/MP3 export only.\n", "sid_model": "8580", "clock": "PAL", "speed": 6, "tempo": 91, "patterns": {"0": {"name": "I